.SH NAME
bpcpd \- ION Delay Tolerant Networking remote file copy daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBbpcpd\fR [\-d | \-v]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBbpcpd\fR is the daemon for \fBbpcp\fR. Together these programs copy files between
hosts utilizing NASA JPL's Interplanetary Overlay Network (ION) to provide a
delay tolerant network.
.PP
The options are permitted as follows:
.Sp
.RS 4
\&\fB \-d\fR	Debug output. Repeat for increased verbosity.
.Sp
\&\fB \-v\fR	Display version information.
.RE
.PP
\&\fBbpcpd\fR must be running in order to copy files from this host to another host
(i.e. remote to local). Copies in the other direction (local to remote) do not
require \fBbpcpd\fR. Further, \fBbpcpd\fR should NOT be run simultaneously with \fBbpcp\fR
or \fBcfdptest\fR.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.IX Header "EXIT STATUS"
.IP """0""" 4
.IX Item """0"""
\&\fBbpcpd\fR terminated normally.
.IP """1""" 4
.IX Item """1"""
\&\fBbpcpd\fR terminated abnormally. Check console and the \fBion.log\fR file for error messages.
.SH FILES
.IX Header "FILES"
No configuration files are needed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IX Header "ENVIRONMENT"
No environment variables apply.
.SH BUGS
.IX Header "BUGS"
Report bugs to <https://github.com/nasa\-jpl/ION\-DTN/issues>
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBbpcp\fR\|(1), \fBion\fR\|(3), \fBcfdptest\fR\|(1)
